SonarQube vs Trivy – Not rivals, but teammates in DevSecOps

In DevOps, security and quality can’t be an afterthought anymore.
Two tools I often see (and use) are SonarQube and Trivy — and they solve very different problems.

🧹 SonarQube – Code Quality & Security
🔍 Scans source code
Finds bugs, code smells, vulnerabilities
Enfores Quality Gates
Stops bad code before merge/deploy
Best placed early in CI
👉 “Is my code clean, secure, and maintainable?”

🛡️ Trivy – Image & Infrastructure Security
🔍 Scans container images, IaC & dependencies
Detects CVEs in OS packages & libraries
Scans Docker images, Kubernetes, Terraform
Lightweight and fast
Best placed before deploy to prod
👉 “Is my runtime environment safe?”

⚖️ Quick comparison
SonarQube → Code-level quality & security
Trivy → Runtime, image & supply-chain security

🚀 Real DevSecOps approach
The strongest pipelines don’t choose one — they use both:
Code → SonarQube → Build → Trivy → Deploy

✔ Clean code
✔ Secure images
✔ Safer production

💡 My takeaway:
SonarQube protects how you write code.
Trivy protects what you run in production.
